rulings.ruling:
Resolved now. A frozen control is an instrument. It never becomes the default on the strength of its own win (C27; the owner's 2026-09-25 ruling, N3).

DEFAULTS:
- `AUD_FREEZE_AT` 0: the codec never stops, so it is live (ON).
- `AUD_FREEZE_AT > 0` stays built as the control arm (03b §6.2 step 9). It runs in the S3 replica and in every S5 plasticity cell, labelled step-matched and compute-matched (03b-16.28).
- Scope: every frozen control of a learned part. Text segmentation at `TOK_RETOK_EVERY` 0 is the one exception: it is read by S0b-ship and escalates under O14.

WHAT COUNTS AS A WIN. Only a win on B's endpoints read after further learning counts. The endpoints are the post-training arrival cell (a held-back family, e.g. aud/chirps, arriving after the main run: arrival speed and BWT) and the within-run cells' worst media area. They are read on codec-invariant readings (01-M3): caption and text-area bits/byte at margin ε; understanding and recover exact at their pre-registered paired-SE margins (note NEW-02). A within-run end-state win (R5) is reported and changes nothing.

IF A FROZEN CONTROL WINS THAT WAY. The live default holds. The live arms already specified are read next on the same cells, least plasticity cost first:
1. `'jit_ema'` codes (03b-16.23);
2. the ceiling guard's 'hold' on calibrated families (03b-16.18);
3. the WiSE-FT-style pull-back at hold expiry (03b-16.18);
4. the OFF arm anchored to a retained release snapshot (03b-16.14);
5. for a large shift, the versioned-block handover (03b-16.21).
The first arm that brings live within the margins of the frozen control becomes the live default (a GPU reading, R0). The frozen control stays an instrument. The question 'is freezing absolutely necessary here?' goes to the owner, with the readings, only if every live arm stays beyond the margins.

